<http://data.silknow.org/object/8c5e5515-bf6f-3397-afe1-19cee5faba63>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Mourning dress, woman's, black silk satin trimmed at the sleeves with lace, British, 1840s, altered in the 1860s"@en , "A front fastening black silk satin dress with short sleeves trimmed with lace.  The skirts are full and pieces of fabric have been added below the waist.  to accommodate the wide 1860s skirts.  The bodice has been altered too.  The alterations are part of the history of the object showing how mourning dress was adapted to the latest fashions."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/4929a909-651e-32e1-a872-65972e192079> ;
